  "worked_solution": "First, to simplify the fraction on the left-hand side, we multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6-7\\text{i}}{3-2\\text{i}} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{(6-7\\text{i})(3+2\\text{i})}{(3-2\\text{i})(3+2\\text{i})} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{18+12\\text{i}-21\\text{i}-14{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{18-9\\text{i}-14(-1)}{13} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{32-9\\text{i}}{13} & =2p-5q\\text{i} \\\\ \\frac{32}{13}-\\frac{9}{13}\\text{i} & =2p-5q\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can equate the real parts and the imaginary parts separately.\n\n- Equating the real parts, we get $\\frac{32}{13}=2p.$\n\n- Equating the imaginary parts, we get $-\\frac{9}{13}=-5q.$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{16}{13}$ and $q=\\frac{9}{65}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
